[CENTER][IMG]https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/8wyK7V60/e6b92fbb3ff1d42e72229b57873a2c0ffc497444.gif[/IMG]

[SIZE=6][B]PvPIndex MCBans[/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4]Global Ban Management for Paper Servers[/SIZE][/CENTER]

[QUOTE]This is a refactored fork of the original [URL='https://dev.bukkit.org/projects/mcbans']MCBans[/URL] plugin. The ban-sharing concept, command structure, and permission layout originate from the MCBans team and their contributors. This fork modernises the codebase for Java 21 / Paper 1.21+ and replaces the legacy MCBans backend with the PvPIndex REST API.[/QUOTE]

[B]PvPIndex MCBans[/B] connects your Paper server to the [URL='https://mcbans.pvpindex.com']mcbans.pvpindex.com[/URL] global ban network. Players banned on any participating server are automatically blocked everywhere else - while you keep full control over local bans, storage backends, and permission levels.

[IMG]https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/8wyK7V60/images/2538f3b59165fa0297e51e61209d0e540cbdfee2_350.webp[/IMG]

[SIZE=5][B]Features[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][B]Global & local bans[/B] - issue a local ban (stays on your server) or a global ban (synced to all connected servers in real time)
[*][B]Temporary bans[/B] - time-limited bans with auto-expiry in minutes, hours, days, or weeks
[*][B]IP bans[/B] - ban by IP address to block VPN abuse and ban evasion
[*][B]VPN detection[/B] - AntVPN WebSocket integration; configurable actions ([ICODE]WARN[/ICODE], [ICODE]KICK[/ICODE], [ICODE]BAN[/ICODE]); [ICODE]mcbans.vpn.bypass[/ICODE] permission lets trusted players skip the check; disabled by default via [ICODE]antivpn.yml[/ICODE]
[*][B]Legacy ban import[/B] - checks mcbans.com for existing bans on player join; results cached locally as [ICODE]is_legacy[/ICODE] records; controlled by the [ICODE]pvpindex.legacy[/ICODE] config section
[*][B]Public kicks[/B] - [ICODE]pvpindex.kicks.public[/ICODE] flag reports kicks to the PvPIndex API and shows them on bans.pvpindex.com
[*][B]Reason presets[/B] - define shorthand keys in config ([ICODE]#hacks[/ICODE], [ICODE]#toxicity[/ICODE]) that expand to full reason strings; extended form supports a [ICODE]default-duration[/ICODE] for temp bans; case-insensitive with tab-completion
[*][B]Customizable kick messages[/B] - per-type templates ([ICODE]global[/ICODE], [ICODE]local[/ICODE], [ICODE]temp[/ICODE], [ICODE]failsafe[/ICODE]) with [ICODE]{reason}[/ICODE], [ICODE]{admin}[/ICODE], [ICODE]{expires}[/ICODE], and [ICODE]{appeal_url}[/ICODE] placeholders
[*][B]Offline resilience[/B] - bans issued during API outages are queued and pushed on recovery; the [ICODE]failsafe[/ICODE] option can also block all banned logins through local database when the API is unreachable
[*][B]Delta sync[/B] - downloads only ban changes on a configurable background interval (default 60 min), keeping the local database lightweight
[*][B]Multiple storage backends[/B] - SQLite (default, zero-config), MySQL/MariaDB, PostgreSQL
[*][B]Alt-account detection[/B] - [ICODE]/altlookup[/ICODE] surfaces known alternate accounts via the PvPIndex API (premium)
[*][B]Developer API (JitPack)[/B] - lightweight [ICODE]pvpindex-mcbans-api[/ICODE] module lets other plugins query ban status without a Bukkit dependency
[*][B]Vault integration[/B] - optional; swap the permission backend to Vault in one config line
[*][B]Fully translatable[/B] - swap the [ICODE]language[/ICODE] key to load a different locale file
[/LIST]

